  "notes": "The small pictures that fly from a monster to where its move's effect plays (steps 1 and 2 of every move's animation): two frames per move whose effect plays away from the user, which alternate while it flies. All in one sheet on purpose: a run already loads ~26 of the 32 sprite sheets the GBA engine can hold, and this adds only one. Each move has its own animation of its two frames (anim_travel_<move>). Every frame keeps a 1 px empty border, so the picture is never cut at the edge of its sprite.",
